       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="GBrowser: Keyboard shortcuts" id="GBrowser-Keyboard-Shortcuts">

    <primary-label ref="gbrowser"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Change shortcuts: <ui-path>Settings | Keymap</ui-path></p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Default keyboard shortcuts of all GBrowser actions, and how to change them in the IDE keymap.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Default shortcuts for every GBrowser action and how to change them.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Default keyboard shortcuts of the GBrowser plugin in JetBrains IDEs, for tabs, navigation, bookmarks and DevTools, and how to reassign them in the keymap.</web-summary>

    <p>
        The table lists the default shortcuts that GBrowser defines for Windows and Linux keymaps.
        macOS keymaps can use other modifier keys.
        On macOS, or to see the shortcut in your current keymap, search for the action name in <ui-path>Settings | Keymap</ui-path>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Default shortcuts" id="default-shortcuts">
        <table>
            <tr>
                <td>Action</td>
                <td>Windows and Linux</td>
            </tr>
            <tr><td><control>Backward</control></td><td><shortcut>Alt+Left</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Forward</control></td><td><shortcut>Alt+Right</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Home</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+H</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Reload Page</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+R</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Stop Loading</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+.</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Find...</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+F</shortcut> or <shortcut>Alt+F3</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Zoom In</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Plus</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Zoom Out</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Minus</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Actual Size</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+0</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Open in Default Browser</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+O</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Open DevTools</control></td><td><shortcut>F12</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Toggle Device Emulation</control> (menu: <control>Emulate Mobile Device Viewport and User Agent</control>)</td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+M</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Add to Bookmarks</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+D</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Bookmark Manager</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+B</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Clear History</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+7</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Clear Cookies</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Shift+8</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Add Tab</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+T</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Close Tab</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+W</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Duplicate Tab</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+D</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Toggle Toolbar Visibility</control></td><td><shortcut>Alt+T</shortcut></td></tr>
            <tr><td><control>Open in GBrowser</control></td><td><shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+G</shortcut></td></tr>
        </table>
        <p>
            <control>Open Selected Text in GBrowser</control>, <control>Preferences</control> and the <control>Bookmarks</control> menu have no default shortcut.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Shortcut conflicts" id="conflicts">
        <p>
            GBrowser shortcuts are part of the IDE keymap, and most GBrowser actions are enabled whenever a GBrowser tab is open, not only when the browser has the focus.
            Several of them, such as <shortcut>Ctrl+D</shortcut>, <shortcut>Ctrl+W</shortcut>, <shortcut>Ctrl+R</shortcut>, <shortcut>Ctrl+F</shortcut> and <shortcut>F12</shortcut>,
            are also assigned to IDE actions.
            If a shortcut does not do what you expect, assign a different one to the GBrowser action or to the IDE action.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Change a shortcut" id="change-shortcut">
        <procedure title="Assign a shortcut to a GBrowser action" id="assign-shortcut">
            <step>
                Open the <control>Settings</control> dialog (<shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+S</shortcut>, macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ,</shortcut>)
                and select <control>Keymap</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Type the action name in the search field, for example <code>Toggle Device Emulation</code>.
                <img src="gbrowser_keymap.png" alt="Keymap settings filtered to GBrowser actions with their shortcuts" width="706" thumbnail="true" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
            <step>
                Right-click the action and select <control>Add Keyboard Shortcut</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Press the new key combination and click <control>OK</control>.
                If the IDE reports a conflict, decide whether to remove the shortcut from the other action.
            </step>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

